  "question": {
    "text": "A charged particle moving with a volocity $\\vec{v}=v_1 \\hat{i}+v_2 \\hat{j}$ in a magnetic field $\\vec{B}$ experiences a force $\\vec{F}=F_1 \\hat{i}+F_2 \\hat{j}$. Here $v_1 \\cdot v_2, F_1, F_2$ all are constants. Then $\\vec{B}$ can be",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "sXWie",
      "text": "$\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{B}}=\\mathrm{B}_1 \\hat{\\mathrm{I}}+\\mathrm{B}_2 \\hat{\\mathrm{j}}$ with $\\frac{\\mathrm{v}_1}{\\mathrm{v}_2}=\\frac{\\mathrm{B}_1}{\\mathrm{~B}_2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SgOuD",
      "text": "$\\vec{B}=B_1 \\hat{i}+B_2 \\hat{j}+B_3 \\hat{k}$ with $\\frac{v_1}{v_2}=\\frac{B_1}{B_2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "cCqaw",
      "text": "$\\vec{B}=B_3 \\hat{j}$ with $B_1=B_2=0$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "bX1ES",
      "text": "$\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{B}}=\\mathrm{B}_1 \\hat{\\mathrm{j}}+\\mathrm{B}_2 \\hat{\\mathrm{k}}$ with $\\frac{\\mathrm{B}_1}{\\mathrm{~B}_2}=\\frac{\\mathrm{v}_1}{\\mathrm{v}_2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hint: $\\vec{F} \\cdot \\vec{V}=0 \\Rightarrow \\frac{F_1}{F_2}=-\\frac{V_2}{V_1} \\ldots \\ldots . .(I)$\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\vec{F} \\cdot \\vec{B}=0 \\Rightarrow \\frac{F_1}{F_2}=-\\frac{B_2}{B_1} \\ldots \\ldots \\ldots .(\\text { (II) } \\\\\n& \\text { Or } \\frac{B_1}{B_2}=\\frac{V_1}{V_2} \\quad \\vec{B}=B_1 \\hat{i}+B_2 \\hat{j}+B_3 \\hat{k}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
